{#
	Pick a template, check the subject, check the address, and send it (XIV-39).

	One form, rendered twice: inside the modal on the record page, and on its own
	page for whoever follows the link rather than opening the modal. Deliberately
	the arrangement the document chooser uses — the modal and the page are one
	description of what a send asks for, rather than two that agree today.

	A select rather than a row of buttons, for the reason the document chooser
	gives: fifty templates on a contact would be fifty buttons.

	**Two submit buttons, and no JavaScript between them.** The form posts to the
	send; "Preview and send" is the same form with a `formaction`, which is plain
	HTML and needs nothing. Sending straight out is what somebody wants on the
	tenth invoice of the morning, and what makes that safe is not a confirmation
	step but the two fields below it: the address and the subject are on the
	screen before the button is pressed.
#}
{% set prefix = id|default('email') %}

<form method="post" action="{{ path('module_email_send', {module: module.key, id: record.id}) }}">
	<input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('send-record-email') }}">

	<div class="mb-3">
		<label class="form-label" for="{{ prefix }}-template">{{ 'mail.template'|trans }}</label>
		<select class="form-select" id="{{ prefix }}-template" name="template" required>
			{% for template in templates %}
				<option value="{{ template.id }}" {{ draft.template == template.id ? 'selected' : '' }}>{{ template.name }}</option>
			{% endfor %}
		</select>
	</div>

	<div class="mb-3">
		<label class="form-label" for="{{ prefix }}-subject">{{ 'mail.subject'|trans }}</label>
		{#
			Left empty on purpose, and the help text says what that means. Nothing
			can fill this box when the select above changes without scripting, and
			a box pre-filled from whichever template happened to be first would be
			a subject silently attached to a different email. Blank and honest
			beats filled and wrong — and it still takes placeholders, so a subject
			typed here is not one that stopped understanding [record_id].
		#}
		<input class="form-control" type="text" id="{{ prefix }}-subject" name="subject"
		       value="{{ draft.subject }}" placeholder="{{ 'mail.subject_placeholder'|trans }}">
		<div class="form-text">{{ 'mail.subject_help'|trans }}</div>
	</div>

	{#
		What goes with it (XIV-40) — the two features meeting, which is "send the
		invoice" and the thing anybody actually wants an ERP to do with an email.

		**Only drawn for somebody who may generate documents as well as send
		mail**, which is why the list arrives empty rather than being filtered
		here: attaching means generating, and a picker offered to whoever lacks
		that grant would be a control that answers 403. The send screen asks the
		same question again when the form comes back, because a form is a POST
		anybody can retype.

		**"Nothing" is the first option and the selected one.** A send with no
		document is the ordinary send, and a box defaulting to whichever template
		happened to be listed first would put a customer's invoice on a mail
		nobody asked to attach one to — the same argument the subject box makes
		one field up, in the direction that matters more.
	#}
	{% if attachments is not empty %}
		<div class="mb-3">
			<label class="form-label" for="{{ prefix }}-document">{{ 'mail.attachment'|trans }}</label>
			<div class="row g-2">
				<div class="col-sm-8">
					<select class="form-select" id="{{ prefix }}-document" name="document">
						<option value="0" {{ draft.document ? '' : 'selected' }}>{{ 'mail.no_attachment'|trans }}</option>
						{% for template in attachments %}
							<option value="{{ template.id }}" {{ draft.document == template.id ? 'selected' : '' }}>{{ template.name }}</option>
						{% endfor %}
					</select>
				</div>
				<div class="col-sm-4">
					<label class="visually-hidden" for="{{ prefix }}-format">{{ 'document.format'|trans }}</label>
					<select class="form-select" id="{{ prefix }}-format" name="format">
						{% for format in formats %}
							<option value="{{ format.value }}" {{ draft.format == format.value ? 'selected' : '' }}>
								{{- ('document.format_' ~ format.value)|trans -}}
							</option>
						{% endfor %}
					</select>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="form-text">{{ 'mail.attachment_help'|trans }}</div>
		</div>
	{% endif %}

	<div class="mb-3">
		<label class="form-label" for="{{ prefix }}-recipient">{{ 'mail.recipient'|trans }}</label>
		{#
			Editable, because a wrong address is not recoverable and whoever presses
			the button is the last check there is. Editing it changes nothing on the
			record: sending one mail somewhere is not a correction to the contact,
			and the help text says so rather than leaving it to be discovered.
		#}
		<input class="form-control" type="email" id="{{ prefix }}-recipient" name="recipient" required
		       value="{{ draft.recipient }}">
		<div class="form-text">
			{{ 'mail.recipient_help'|trans }}
			{% if recipient.viaLabel %}
				{{ 'mail.recipient_from_link'|trans({'%via%': recipient.viaLabel, '%field%': recipient.fieldLabel}) }}
			{% elseif recipient.fieldLabel %}
				{{ 'mail.recipient_from_field'|trans({'%field%': recipient.fieldLabel}) }}
			{% endif %}
		</div>
	</div>

	<div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">
		<button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">
			<i class="bi bi-send" aria-hidden="true"></i> {{ 'mail.send'|trans }}
		</button>
		<button class="btn btn-outline-secondary" type="submit"
		        formaction="{{ path('module_email_preview', {module: module.key, id: record.id}) }}">
			<i class="bi bi-eye" aria-hidden="true"></i> {{ 'mail.preview_and_send'|trans }}
		</button>
	</div>
</form>
